  message: "SATISFIED by PR #1685 (dev f18f16d9c7): a dated module_completeness entry for threading.Event in io_primitives/python.yaml (set/clear/is_set/wait are in-process). Evidence, the item's own repro re-run locally on the fixed tree with check-self-claims' exact invocation (python -m hypergumbo_core verify-claims . --claims docs/hypergumbo.claims.yaml --json --minimal): rc 3, 18/18 confirmed_with_caveats, opaque_boundary present on all 18, no 'could not classify' clause; scripts/check-self-claims-drift <run> docs/hypergumbo.claims.expected.json -> 'OK -- 18 claims unchanged (18 confirmed_with_caveats)', exit 0. Before the fix, the same command on 8bc23ede1d reproduced CI's 36-line drift exactly, and the verdict detail named the blocker: 'calls into 1 module(s) that the I/O catalog could not classify (threading.Event)'. The snapshot was not touched. Residual: the cron self-claims-gate has not fired since the merge; the next full-suite run is the on-CI confirmation. Observation for the owner, not filed: this is the fourth time a newly typed class-qualified stdlib receiver flipped all 18 claims, and detection is bounded by the 12 h cron since the per-PR arm was removed."  # 0a92
